  "p1": [
    "The frozen recovery contract r3 still contains pre-DC forecast fields for the superseded DC runner SHA and the nonexistent vcs_hammer review path. It never authorized DC; this review and admission explicitly bind the final runner and actual vcs_receipt_hammer path. Do not cite the forecast fields as final identities.",
    "OPT-150 is an immediate pre-ungroup abort only when emitted in precompile check_timing. Any OPT-150 emitted later is still fail-closed by the full dc.log scan, but only after dc_shell exits; do not overstate an all-phase immediate OPT-150 gate.",
    "The completed DC tree uses a full-file manifest but no predeclared dynamic filename or symlink whitelist, and receipt JSON generation does not set allow_nan=false explicitly. A receipt-blind review must independently check exact topology, confined symlinks, strict finite JSON and every report before citation."
  ],
  "p2": [
    "Process collision checks are sampled before each point and at finalization rather than protected by a host-global lock; a foreign EDA process starting mid-point remains a residual race that the receipt review must inspect in resource logs.",
    "There is a narrow external-writer race between the final canonical absence check and mv -T after m485_complete becomes one. The attempt marker prevents a second conforming M519 runner, but unrelated manual writes to the canonical path remain outside the runner's authority.",
    "The final fairness gate compares reported port counts rather than report_port schemas. Because all three elaborations share the exact same declared top and pins this is non-blocking, but the receipt review should diff normalized port reports."
  ]
